<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady on increased arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady on increased arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained steady in central Indian markets on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Purchasing from processing plants was good against increased arrivals, anmounting to around 8,000 tonnes in the markets of central India.</p>
<p>The undertone was steady. Soyoil prices were down by 100 rupees per tonne on limited demand in local markets. Business was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained at almost the previous level in thin trading. Soymeal yellow was $280-281 per tonne in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $122 FOR ready shipment and was $115 per tonne for March-April shipment in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,250 rupees FOR Bedi Bunder and was 4,200 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
